\chapter{Global System Synthesis and Unified Engine Manifold of the Temporal Symmetry Systems Engine (TSSE)}
\section{Overview}

Chapter 11 formalizes the Global System Synthesis and Unified Engine Manifold of the
Temporal Symmetry Systems Engine (TSSE). Building upon the axioms, Hamiltonian
foundations, relativistic propulsion kernels, fusion energetic kernels, structural
invariant computation, verification formalism, stability regimes, and autonomous
control architecture established in Chapters 1–10, this chapter defines the global
integration of all TSSE subsystems into a single unified manifold and synthesizes
the complete TSSE engine architecture.

The TSSE Global System Synthesis (TSSE-GSS) governs:
\begin{enumerate}
  \item The unified manifold construction across all TSSE subsystems.
  \item The global Hamiltonian and its invariant-preserving structure.
  \item The synthesis operator for subsystem integration.
  \item The global evolution operator and its symplectic properties.
  \item The canonical TSSE Unified Engine Kernel (TSSE-UEK).
\end{enumerate}

This chapter establishes the complete mathematical and structural blueprint for
the unified TSSE engine.

