\section{Unified TSSE Manifold Construction}

Let $\mathcal{S}_{i}$ denote the structural manifold of subsystem $i$:
\[
\mathcal{S}_{\text{T}},\;
\mathcal{S}_{\text{RPK}},\;
\mathcal{S}_{\text{FK}},\;
\mathcal{S}_{\text{SIK}},\;
\mathcal{S}_{\text{VK}},\;
\mathcal{S}_{\text{SK}},\;
\mathcal{S}_{\text{CK}}.
\]

Define the unified manifold:
\[
\mathcal{S}_{\text{TSSE}} =
\prod_{i=1}^{7} \mathcal{S}_{i}.
\]

\begin{definition}[Unified TSSE Manifold]
The unified TSSE manifold is the direct product of all subsystem manifolds and
represents the complete structural domain of the TSSE engine.
\end{definition}

\begin{lemma}[Unified Manifold Closure]
If each $\mathcal{S}_{i}$ is closed under its subsystem evolution, then:
\[
\mathcal{U}(t)\mathcal{S}_{\text{TSSE}} = \mathcal{S}_{\text{TSSE}}.
\]
\end{lemma}

\begin{proof}
Since $\mathcal{U}(t)$ acts independently on each subsystem manifold and each
manifold is closed, the direct product is closed.
\end{proof}

This lemma establishes the global structural stability of the unified TSSE engine.

