\section{Global TSSE Hamiltonian}

Let $H_{i}$ denote the Hamiltonian of subsystem $i$:
\[
H_{\text{T}},\;
H_{\text{RPK}},\;
H_{\text{FK}},\;
H_{\text{SIK}},\;
H_{\text{VK}},\;
H_{\text{SK}},\;
H_{\text{CK}}.
\]

Define the global Hamiltonian:
\[
H_{\text{TSSE}} = \sum_{i=1}^{7} H_{i}.
\]

\begin{definition}[Global TSSE Hamiltonian]
The global TSSE Hamiltonian is the sum of all subsystem Hamiltonians and governs
the complete evolution of the unified TSSE engine.
\end{definition}

\begin{lemma}[Hamiltonian Additivity]
If each $H_{i}$ is TSSE-admissible, then $H_{\text{TSSE}}$ is TSSE-admissible.
\end{lemma}

\begin{proof}
TSSE admissibility requires commutation with $\mathcal{T}$, symplectic evolution,
and manifold closure. Each property is preserved under Hamiltonian addition.
\end{proof}

\begin{theorem}[Global Hamiltonian Admissibility]
The unified TSSE engine evolves under a TSSE-admissible Hamiltonian.
\end{theorem}

\begin{proof}
Follows from subsystem admissibility and Hamiltonian additivity.
\end{proof}

This theorem establishes the global Hamiltonian foundation of the unified engine.

