\section{Global Evolution Operator}

Let $\mathcal{U}_{i}(t)$ denote the evolution operator of subsystem $i$. Define the
global evolution operator:
\[
\mathcal{U}_{\text{TSSE}}(t) =
\prod_{i=1}^{7} \mathcal{U}_{i}(t).
\]

\begin{definition}[Global TSSE Evolution Operator]
The global TSSE evolution operator is the product of all subsystem evolution
operators and governs the complete evolution of the unified TSSE engine.
\end{definition}

\begin{lemma}[Symplectic Global Evolution]
If each $\mathcal{U}_{i}(t)$ is symplectic, then:
\[
\mathcal{U}_{\text{TSSE}}(t)^\top J\,\mathcal{U}_{\text{TSSE}}(t) = J.
\]
\end{lemma}

\begin{proof}
The product of symplectic matrices is symplectic.
\end{proof}

\begin{theorem}[Global Invariant Preservation]
The unified TSSE evolution operator preserves all TSSE invariants.
\end{theorem}

\begin{proof}
Invariant preservation follows from symplecticity, Hamiltonian consistency, and
manifold closure.
\end{proof}

This theorem establishes the global invariant-preserving evolution of the unified engine.

